  "comments": "<p>Coins 1976-2007 are minted in Stockholm (AB Tumba Bruk Myntverket / AB Svenska Myntverket, Stockholm / Eskilstuna)<br>Coins from 2008 and 2009 are minted in Vantaa, Finland.</p><p><br><i>Main groups of style</i><br><br><i>Reverse</i><br>Die <strong>A</strong> - top rays of the left star connects high.<br>Die <strong>B</strong> - stars have deep cut rays.<br>Die <strong>C</strong> - stars have bold rays connected far from center.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/616e97e992d8f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/616e97e992d8f.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>A</strong>: 1976-1986, 1991 E U.<br><strong>B</strong>: 1987-1990, 1991 E D, 1992-2007.<br><strong>C</strong>: 2008, 2009.<br><br><i>Note</i>. The style of dies indicates that the issue of 1991 E U was made with the die <strong>A</strong> of reverse, which most probably mean, that it was used by mistake, and not that the minting was under supervision of mint official Benkt Ulvfot.<br><br>Krause's \"Standard Catalog of World Coins\" makes a difference between coins minted 1976-1992 (KM# 853) and 1993-2009 (KM# 853a), but it is unclear on which grounds, as the Swedish Riksbank does not recognize any changes in composition.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/65b3e6069f812.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/65b3e6069f812.jpg\"></a></p>",
